        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Algorithm 2 summarizes one recursive step, launched with $\\mathcal{N} = \\{1, \\ldots, n\\}$ and $d = 0$. Each internal node fits one twoblock split model (and, under per-node cross-validation, a small grid of them); with the matrix-free coskewness solver of Section 3.3 the per-node cost stays of the same order as the covariance fit. Once the structure is fixed, each of the $|\\mathcal{L}(\\mathcal{T})|$ leaves is refit once under the covariance leaf objective – a cheap ordinary twoblock fit on the leaf's",
